y5-compositor (1.4.1-1ubuntu2) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Restore the monitor frontend shell (logs/dist/index.html) deleted by
    mistake in an unrelated commit; y5-compositor-monitor showed an empty
    window without it.
  * vendor-all: refuse stale Cargo.lock instead of silently regenerating it
    during vendoring; lockfile updates must be reviewed commits.
  * rules: honour DEB_BUILD_OPTIONS parallel=N via CARGO_BUILD_JOBS
    (conservative default 2) to avoid OOM on Launchpad builders.
  * rules: dh_installsystemduser --no-enable so user units are never enabled
    globally (they would start Y5 inside GNOME/KDE sessions).
  * build-bundle: compile all Cargo components into the shared target dir;
    unset RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN properly; add relro/bindnow link hardening.
  * y5.service: start y5.shutdown.target on stop so leftover session units
    (polkit agent) are torn down on logout.
  * control: y5-compositor-settings is a hard Depends; drop xwayland from
    the core package (owned by y5-xwayland-satellite).
  * session: seed a complete default settings.json on first start via
    `y5.compositor.settings --write-default` (the upstream canonical
    template) instead of refusing to launch; an existing file is never
    touched.
  * Track mx-gesture-daemon's Cargo.lock in git (a library-style local
    .gitignore hid it); the orig previously shipped without it, which
    would have failed `cargo build --frozen` on Launchpad.
  * source/options: extend-diff-ignore the gitignored Tauri build
    outputs (dist bundles, src-tauri/gen) so a source build after a
    binary build does not fail on "unexpected upstream changes".
  * postinst: purge stale global user-unit enablement left by pre-split
    local builds, which auto-started y5 inside other desktops.
  * source/options: replace misleading tar-ignore entries for the vendor
    trees with extend-diff-ignore (they are a required part of the orig).
  * make-orig: verify VERSION matches the debian/changelog version.
  * upload-ppa: refuse dirty working trees when creating the orig.
  * build-docker/upload-ppa: restore file ownership after container builds.
  * bundle-rust-toolchain: pin the bundled rustc version and record it.
  * copyright: document rust-toolchain-dist/ licensing.
  * Update maintainer e-mail; drop the no-op y5-compositor.postinst.

 -- Kacper Paczos <kacperpaczos2024@protonmail.com>  Thu, 16 Jul 2026 19:30:00 +0200

